HIGH: Bridge Withdrawer Identity Spoof: function 'emergencyWithdraw' in contract 0x965d3704de812f5e1e7eef1ac22fe92174258bd9 on BNB Chain

Withdrawer identity spoof: the bridge release pays a recipient taken straight from the call parameters, and the recipient is not bound to any deposit record or signed message hash in the function - whoever submits the withdrawal names the payee, so a watcher can redirect other users' releases to themselves.

Code:
function emergencyWithdraw(
        IERC20 _token,
        address _to,
        uint256 _amount
    ) external onlyOwner {
        require(address(0) != _to, "MXY: transfer to the zero address");
        if (_token == IERC20(address(0))) {
            (bool success, ) = _to.call{value: _amount}("");
            require(success, "MXY: Transfer failed");
        } else {
            _token.safeTransfer(_to, _amount);
        }
    }

