HIGH: Eip712 Separator Unbound: function 'delegateBySig' in contract 0x810ee35443639348adbbc467b33310d2ab43c168 on BNB Chain

EIP-712 domain separator not bound to the live chain: the separator used by a signature / permit path is cached once (constructor, immutable or state variable) and never recomputed from block.chainid at verify time, or it is constructed with no chainId term at all. After a chain fork - or on any chain where the contract is redeployed at the same address - signatures replay across chains because the separator no longer distinguishes them. Observed: 'delegateBySig' verifies against a domain separator that is constructed with no chainId term. Recipient analysis: recipient classified UNRESOLVED (no value destination found in function) - a stranger can receive value or control here, classified CANDIDATE under the receive rule.

Code:
function delegateBySig(address delegatee, uint nonce, uint expiry, uint8 v, bytes32 r, bytes32 s) public {
        bytes32 domainSeparator = keccak256(abi.encode(DOMAIN_TYPEHASH, keccak256(bytes(name)), uint(0), address(this)));
        bytes32 structHash = keccak256(abi.encode(DELEGATION_TYPEHASH, delegatee, nonce, expiry));
        bytes32 digest = keccak256(abi.encodePacked("\x19\x01", domainSeparator, structHash));
        address signatory = ecrecover(digest, v, r, s);
        require(signatory != address(0), "delegateBySig: invalid signature");
        require(nonce == nonces[signatory]++, "delegateBySig: invalid nonce");
        require(now <= expiry, "delegateBySig: signature expired");
        return _delegate(signatory, delegatee);
    }

